      "info": "Set in the pixel face and uppercased. Keep it short — it loses its grid in long sentences.",
      "default": "One deal. One day. Blink and it's someone else's."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body_2",
      "label": "Body — after the pull quote",
      "default": "<p>We call it the Yoink of the Day, because yoink is the sound of grabbing something great half a second before the person next to you.</p><p>Nature's already full of professionals at this. Raccoons yoink the dog food. Seagulls yoink the fries. Bears yoink the whole picnic basket and don't even say thank you. We're just doing it with better taste and free-ish shipping — a little retail Robin Hood move where somehow everybody wins: you get the score, the good stuff finds its people, and we get to keep the lights on.</p><p>To be clear, we are not out here trying to buy a yacht. A canoe, maybe. We're just making the most of the hand we've been dealt — and, conveniently, dealing is kind of our whole thing. Mostly we like tracking down cool stuff for cheap and handing you the deal like it's a dare. Some days the Yoink is exactly what you didn't know you needed. Some days it's a penguin-shaped thing that is very much Not For You — no notes, there's a new one tomorrow.</p><p>So stick around. Watch the drops. Rummage the Bargain Bin between yoinks. And when the good one hits — you know what to do.</p>"
